# Data & API

## Layer structure

1. Paths → `src/data/client/endpoints.ts` (`API_ENDPOINTS.TASKS`, etc.)
2. HTTP methods → `src/data/client/index.ts`
3. Hooks → one domain file under `src/data/` (`task.ts`, `auth.ts`)

## Queries

```tsx
export const useTasks = (params = {}, options?) => {
  const { data, isPending, isError, error, refetch } = useFilteredQuery({
    queryKeyPrefix: [API_ENDPOINTS.TASKS],
    queryFn: (params) => client.tasks.all(params),
    params,
    ...options,
  });
  return { tasks: data ?? [], isPending, isError, error, refetch };
};
```

- Filtered lists: `useFilteredQuery` / `useFilteredInfiniteQuery` from `src/lib/hooks/`
- Keys always include `API_ENDPOINTS` constants

## Mutations

- Use project **`useMutation`** from `src/lib/hooks/use-mutation.ts` (not raw React Query)
- Set `invalidateQueryFilter` for cache invalidation
- `onError`: `toast.error({ message: renderError(error) })`
- `onSuccess`: translated toast via `t('object-created', { ... })`

## Don't

- Hardcode API paths
- Call `axios` directly outside the client layer
